### Goal Model Decomposition

Below is the goal model decomposition based on the mission description provided. The goal model is structured using the AND/OR decomposition rules and the specified runtime annotations.

---

### Goal Table

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition** / **Enquired Information** | **Relation** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------|--------------|
| **G1**   | Deliver resources to the requesting agent | "-" | Achieve | The resources are delivered to the specified location | - |
| **G2**   | Collect resources from storage locations | "#" | Perform | All requested resources are collected | AND |
| **G3**   | Deliver collected resources to the specified location | "-" | Perform | All resources are delivered to the specified location | AND |
| **G4**   | Handle low battery during collection phase | "-" | Perform | The robot returns to the recharging station and assigns the mission to another robot | AND |
| **G5**   | Handle low battery during delivery phase | "-" | Perform | The robot returns to the checkpoint and assigns the remaining task to another robot | AND |
| **G6**   | Trigger alert for failed resource return | "-" | Perform | An alert is sent to the sector manager | AND |
| **G7**   | Assign multiple robots for parallel collection | "-" | Perform | Multiple robots are assigned to collect resources from different storage locations | AND |

